# Proofs of glam/LOOP_LAWS.bend (cursor-laws.loop), kept by hand.
#
# Lessons:
# - A law over code that writes a heap goes through the view: the code's
#   heap equated to sets on the words (XP.alloc_eq for P.node, the writes
#   by computation once a static test is rewritten away), each set's view
#   a List.set of the one before (LA.set_view, the words kept full by
#   LA.set_full), so that the invariant is proved over the list form
#   alone (px_sv), a Data term, with no heap in it.
# - A conjunct that reads a written word is proved at the value written
#   and carried to the read by ME.subst, its motive the conjunct with the
#   read a hole (faces, px.off, px.tw in px_sv).
# - An index the checker cannot compute (P.node.word of a header whose
#   level is a variable) is split by its test, a Bool matched first, each
#   case calling one body with the index as a parameter (ws_at(s, pi)).
# - Two nodes of a list laid out apart, not the same, are four words apart
#   wherever they stand in it (lay_pair): the one met first crosses every
#   later one, the induction passed as a function of the tail's
#   memberships.

